course: dictionary
lesson: 1990
title: Reading a hard word in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Compsognathus is a long word, but the sentences around it give you clues. «Compsognathus was about 1 metre long including its tail.» The sentence tells you the word names something with a size, so you can read on and learn more.
explain: The second sentence gives a clear clue: «from the chicken-sized Compsognathus to Diplodocus, longer than two buses». Compared with buses and Diplodocus, it must be small. Try it: swap in "small dinosaur" for the hard word. Does the sentence still make sense? It does, so your guess is right.
explain: You do not need to say every letter of a long word perfectly to understand it. Read the whole sentence, look for clues, and then check the meaning in the facts.
fact: Compsognathus was a small meat-eating dinosaur about the size of a chicken or turkey.
fact: It ran on two legs and lived about 150 million years ago in what is now Germany and France.
fact: The name Compsognathus means «pretty jaw».
fact: One fossil was found with a lizard in its stomach, which showed what it ate.
fact: In films it is often shortened to «compy».
exercise: «Compsognathus was about 1 metre long including its tail.» What does this sentence tell you? | *It was about 1 metre long, tail included | It weighed one tonne | It could fly over the sea | It was 1 metre tall, without its tail
exercise: «From the chicken-sized Compsognathus to Diplodocus, longer than two buses.» What size was Compsognathus compared with a chicken? | As long as two buses | Much bigger than a house | *About the same size as a chicken | Bigger than Diplodocus
exercise: Films often say «compy». What does this mean? | A kind of fossil | A chicken farm | A type of bird that lives in Germany | *A shortened name for Compsognathus
test: What kind of food did Compsognathus eat? | Nuts and seeds | Plants and leaves | Fish only | *Meat
test: Where did Compsognathus live? | In Scotland | In the Arctic | *In what is now Germany and France | In Australia
exam: What does the name Compsognathus mean? | Fast runner | Big teeth | *Pretty jaw | Little chicken
